Changelog: 22-11-2026 21:58:22

Release 1.8.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 21:22:28

Added. Exit RPCS3 is the first button under the games table. It ends RPCS3 at once, with everything it started, and asks
nothing first. It is on only while RPCS3 runs. A game that runs ends without saving, as its tooltip says. The line under
the tabs then says "RPCS3 was ended." The app finds RPCS3's processes with core's new processes module. The wiki chapter
has a new section, Exit RPCS3.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 20:00:16

Release 1.7.1.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 15:55:10

Fixed. The app's files that had no license line have one now, the arrow of its lists among them.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 15:19:54

Fixed. The states beside the title now use two colors: green when all is well, red when not. A warning and an off state,
such as Not installed or shadNet Off, are red now. The wiki says so.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 12:25:09

Release 1.7.0.

Changelog: 22-11-2026 11:44:56

Added. The row beside the title has a new state, Steam. Its dot is green while Steam runs and is signed in, and red when
it is not, because a game in Steam starts only then. The app looks again every few seconds. The states now show their
names alone, Installed, RPCN, Controller and Steam, and the dot's color shows the state. Each tooltip opens with the
state in full, such as Not installed or No controller. The wiki describes the row. test_main_window.py tests the Steam
state and follows the new order.

Changelog: 21-11-2026 12:04:44

Release 1.6.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 19:26:09

Release 1.5.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 18:49:20

Added. The window's new order (owner, 20-11-2026: shadPS4 Manager's design in every manager). The header's pills are
the RPCS3 version, RPCS3 Install, RPCS3 Uninstall and Refresh. The row under them is Games Install, Games Uninstall,
Available in Steam, RPCN Account and Play time. Games Uninstall is new: it is what the Remove game… button under the
table did, and that button went. The Your games box went. Under the pills are two columns: the five state lines,
each name with a colon (RPCS3:, Firmware:, Disc games:, PKG games:, RPCN:), and beside them Installed version:, the
RPCS3 version in use. The tabs are Your games, Start game, Memory cards, Settings, View logs (it was Log) and Clear
logs.

Added. A check for a game that is in Steam more than once. The app says which games and how often, the game's In
Steam box says it in its tooltip, and Update Steam lights and leaves one shortcut of each, with the latest play
time; its question says how many double shortcuts go.

Fixed. The chosen row of a table is 30 % blue, with the theme's text color: filled with the header's blue, a chosen
first row could hardly be told from the header above it.

Fixed. Start game with Steam closed started Steam and never the game, while the line said "Steam starts" (seen in
shadPS4 Manager on the board, 20-11-2026). The app now starts Steam first, waits until it takes commands, then gives
it the game's address, again when the game does not come up (core's play). The line says the game runs only once
RPCS3 does, and says when Steam did not start it. While RPCS3 runs already, Start game starts no second one.

Fixed. A shortcut whose fields Steam wrote in lower case (exe, launchoptions) was not recognized as the app's, so
Update Steam added the game a second time. They are read whatever their case now.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 13:11:18

Release 1.4.0.

Changelog: 20-11-2026 03:39:29

Added. The version manager (owner, 20-11-2026: as shadPS4's own launcher has one; core's builds). The version box in
the header is a pill: its menu lists the RPCS3 builds installed and puts another in use, and Manage versions… opens
the version manager, which downloads RPCS3's newest build (GitHub lists its builds by name, not by date, so only the
newest) from GitHub, checked against the SHA-256 GitHub publishes, adds a custom AppImage, puts a build in use and
deletes one. Builds stay side by side: Install no longer deletes the others, and puts the build this version was tried
with back in use, without a download when it is still there. Uninstall removes every build. A build other than the
tested one is said to be not tried on the board.

Changelog: 19-11-2026 22:33:16

Release 1.3.1.

Changelog: 19-11-2026 22:12:37

Fixed. The message about a newer build says it comes once it has been tried on the board, not the console (owner, 19-11-2026: board everywhere).

Changelog: 18-11-2026 04:15:16

Release 1.3.0.

Changelog: 18-11-2026 03:13:06

Added. RPCN, RPCS3's online service, as shadPS4 Manager has shadNet: an RPCN Account pill opens a window that
creates an account on an RPCN server, tries a sign-in, has the token mailed again and saves the account in RPCS3's
own files, so RPCS3 signs in when a game starts. An RPCN line names the account that signs in, and beside the app's
state stands RPCN Off, Online or Offline. The password is kept and sent as RPCS3 derives it, never as typed.

Changelog: 18-11-2026 02:32:46

Added. The managers' new design, as PPSSPP Manager's and PCSX2 Manager's: a Memory cards tab with the saves on
RPCS3's hard disk (export to a .zip, import, delete). Clear logs, a tab beside Log that is a button, empties the
app's log file and the Log tab and removes the older log files. Start game stands beside Your games. The six tabs
share the window's whole width and are pills as the ones above them. Play time moved from the header to the row
of action pills. Under the header's pills only the links to RPCS3's release notes and the wiki are left, in the
type of a pill's caption; the introduction went. RPCS3's state is one line, and the Firmware line is the version alone, or Uninstalled. Under the games an info symbol stands
in for the line of text about Steam. The window opens 900 wide (it was 980), which is its narrowest, and 606 high
(it was 800); the Settings tab scrolls when it is higher than the window.

Changelog: 17-11-2026 14:53:56

Release 1.2.0.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 11:26:39

Release 1.1.0.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 10:16:55

Fixed. Escape and a controller's B are core's exit_keys (the app's own copy is gone): B closes the window only once
the app has had the focus for half a second, so the press that closed another app does not close this one too; a
dialog and a menu keep their own Escape. Start game is core's ActionTab: the arrow keys and Ctrl+Tab pass it by, only a click on it starts the game.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 07:43:15

Release 1.0.2.

Changelog: 15-11-2026 03:22:26

Fixed. The uninstall on a computer where the app is not installed says so ("… is not installed: nothing to remove.")
and stops, without asking for the sudo password; it listed its removal steps for what was never there (owner,
15-11-2026). With anything of the app there, it uninstalls as before.

